    "budgetW": 370,
    "sourceUrl": "https://www.h3c.com/en/Support/Resource_Center/EN/Switches/Catalog/S5130S/S5130S-EI/Technical_Documents/Product_Literature/Hardware_Information___Specifications/H3C_S5130S-EI_IG/202306/1867335_294551_0.htm",
    "note": "370 W total PoE power shared by the 24 PoE ports: 90 W a port on ports 1-8 (802.3bt PoE++) and 30 W on ports 9-24. The vendor PoE table prints 24 ports at 15.4 W, 12 at 30 W, 6 at 60 W and 4 at 90 W, so the 370 W block caps the eight 90 W ports at four at full power."
  },
  "fabric": {
    "capacityMbps": 128000,
    "kind": "switching fabric",
    "note": "Port switching capacity 128 Gbps (24 x 1G + 4 x 10G, full duplex), forwarding capacity 95.2 Mpps, 1.5 MB packet buffer."
  },
  "sourceUrl": "https://www.h3c.com/en/Products_and_Solutions/InterConnect/Switches/Products/Campus_Network/Access/S5130/H3C_S5130S_EI/",
  "notes": "S5130S-EI common platform (Comware 7): box switching capacity 336 Gbps, 256 MB flash / 512 MB SDRAM, IRF2 stacking of up to 9 units, static routes plus RIP and OSPF, 802.1Q VLAN, LACP, STP/RSTP/MSTP, DHCP server, SNMPv1/v2c/v3, NETCONF/gRPC, web UI and CLI. Port layout and PoE totals from the vendor hardware-information page (https://www.h3c.com/en/Support/Resource_Center/EN/Switches/Catalog/S5130S/S5130S-EI/Technical_Documents/Product_Literature/Hardware_Information___Specifications/H3C_S5130S-EI_IG/202306/1867335_294551_0.htm); switching and forwarding figures from the vendor product page (https://www.h3c.com/en/Products_and_Solutions/InterConnect/Switches/Products/Campus_Network/Access/S5130/H3C_S5130S_EI/). Current software line is Comware 7 CMW710, release R6381 listed on the H3C resource centre for this series (https://www.h3c.com/en/Support/Resource_Center/EN/Switches/Catalog/S5130S/S5130S-EI/default.htm). Fanless (0 dB per ISO 7779), 440 x 422 x 43.6 mm, <= 6 kg, 12 W minimum / 400 W maximum draw. Two port classes on one chassis: ports 1-8 are 802.3bt PoE++ PSE, ports 9-24 are 802.3at PoE+. Serial console plus micro USB console, 80 Gbps maximum stacking bandwidth."
